  "decision": "No default change. A target process memory limit, required headroom, isolated HTTP process measurements and repeated runs are required before sizing.",
  "limitations": [
    "The diagnostic checkpoint intentionally prolongs capture, DOM, transformed stream and output coexistence.",
    "HTTP API, gateway and client share one process, so HTTP memory is observational rather than gateway-isolated.",
    "Loopback omits TLS, authentication, remote network behavior, exporters and production clients.",
    "Forced GC changes runtime state; working set and private bytes need not return to baseline.",
